<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guido Torelli</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1379–1449</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guido Torelli was an Italian condottiere who served the Visconti dukes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> and commanded their forces in several wars. In 1406 he received the town of Guastalla on the Po, later raised to a county, and he also held Montechiarugolo. His descendants ruled Guastalla until 1539, when it was sold to Ferrante Gonzaga.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guido-torelli.jpg" alt="Guido Torelli" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pramzan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guido_Torelli.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
